  "hints": [
    "Search by location and dates is a different workload from showing one listing. Give it its own service and data store.",
    "Booking specific nights is the classic race: check availability, then write. Lock the room.",
    "Client \u2192 CDN, and Client \u2192 LB (2) \u2192 Search Service (2) \u2192 Elasticsearch (2), and \u2192 Booking Service (2) \u2192 Cache + Postgres (2). Both services \u2192 Redis Lock (2)."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 45,
    "costBudget": 1600
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Search runs on a geo-aware index (Elasticsearch geo queries) with date availability as a filter, and is kept in sync from the bookings database.",
    "Bookings live in SQL, where a unique constraint on (room, night) is the final guard against double-booking. The lock just makes conflicts rare and fast to resolve.",
    "Listing pages are read-heavy and cacheable; photos belong on a CDN."
  ]
